{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>As he drew near.</b> His camp, in the manner of \"and Pharaoh drew near\"." "<b>Now I know.</b> Rashi interpreted, and similar to it is \"turn aside, please,\" regarding Lot. That is, these two instances of נא are not like the rest of the נא in Scripture, whose meaning is an expression of request; these two נא mean an expression of now." "<b>That a beautiful woman you are.</b> It refers after it, that is, <b>Now I know</b> — on account of \"that a beautiful woman you are.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:00.182778046Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}